anding  job and i know that they appreciate the  rams um the way that they handled it as  well and we just we had minimal contact  and got through the super bowl and then  hit the ground running when monday came  around  hey one last question for you before i  let you get back to work you know  bengals fans they were spoiled by five  straight years of playoff appearances  although disappointed by no playoff wins  has been kind of a malaise around the  team the past few years what do you say  to win those fans over fill up the  stadium get people engaged in the  bengals moving forward  well i don't want to make any bold  predictions but what i can tell them is  that we're going to build this culture  here in this building one day at a time  it's by having the right people that are  around our players having the right  players in the building and setting high  standards for these guys and it'll be  it'll be clear from day one when they  walk in the building so now we certainly  feel like our schemes are going to be  very sound and  uh creative and you know so we're going  to push the envelope in that regard um i  think by the first time that it rolls  around i think these fans will fill  these seats and be excited to see what  we can put on the field because we'll be  prepared we'll be ready and it'll be an  exciting time for all of us  exciting times and busy times coach i  know things don't slow down for you  until the middle of june at the earliest  we wish you all the best as you make the  transition congratulations on your  success look forward to seeing you at  the combine and talking to you soon  you bet mike thanks for having me on  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

